  "body": "picture element in microdata\r\n\r\n1. The setence of following should be added to the section of 5.2.4 Values.\r\n```\r\n If the element is a `picture` element\r\n   The value is foobar.\r\n If the element is a `source` element whose parent is `picture` element\r\n   The value is foobar.\r\n```\r\n  \r\nBecause `picture` element doesn't have the element's descendant text content, and `source` element whose parent is `picture` element doesn't have `src` attriute.\r\nWhat to do with *foobar* must be considered. As an example, the value of `src` attribute of `img` element who is child of the `picture` element can be considered.\r\n  \r\n  \r\nOr,\r\n2. The setence of following should be added.\r\n> A `itemprop` attribute must not be specified on `picture` element and `source` element whose parent is `picture` element.\r\n  \r\nBecause it is enough if `img` element who is child of the `picture` element has `itemprop` attribute and `src` attribute.\r\n",
